      "content": "That's a solid start, it actually reads quite naturally. Thanks for keeping the scientific tone.\n\nThe thing is, I just ran this through a local version of the scoring tool and the density score came back really low—like 0.03. I'm worried that even if the human reviewers like it, the automated filter might flag it as \"low relevance\" and toss it before a human even touches it. \n\nCould you try to beef it up a bit? I don't want you to make it nonsensical, but we probably need to hit a higher density to be safe. Try to integrate the keywords more deeply into the technical arguments rather than just listing them. Aim for a bit more \"thematic weight\" while still keeping it professional.",
